<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What this app is allowed to talk to, and how.

    Nothing goes over plain HTTP. The app makes exactly three kinds of request: a WebDAV sync to
    somebody's own server, and two food lookups. All three carry either a password or a record of
    what somebody eats, and none of them has any business travelling in the clear. Blocked here
    rather than left to each call site, because a call site can be added and a policy cannot be
    forgotten.

    Certificates are the public ones the phone ships with, and nothing else. A Nextcloud on
    somebody's own network usually signs its own, which is why the app lets them pick that
    certificate and trusts it at the socket instead: a trust anchor named here would have to be
    built into the app, and a person cannot put their own server's certificate into a release.
    See PinnedTrust.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
